.Dd July 8, 2026
.Dt PMC.LBR 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pmc.lbr
.Nd Last Branch Record capture for
.Tn AMD
CPUs
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libpmc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In pmc.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
AMD Zen 4 and newer processors implement LBR v2
.Pq LbrExtV2 ,
a per-core ring of the most recent taken branches recorded as
From/To address pairs.
The ring holds 16 records on current parts; the detected depth is
reported by the
.Va kern.hwpmc.amd_lbr_depth
sysctl.
On CPUs with the LbrAndPmcFreeze feature the ring freezes when a core
counter overflows, so the records describe the branches leading up to
each sampling interrupt; see
.Sx CAVEATS
for hardware without it.
.Pp
LBR capture is not a PMC class of its own.
It is requested with the
.Li lbr
event qualifier on a core counter allocated in sampling mode, for
example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pmcstat -S ex_ret_brn_tkn,lbr -O sample.out command
.Ed
.Pp
Allocation fails when the CPU does not implement LbrExtV2, when the
PMC is not a core counter, or when it is not in sampling mode.
The
.Li usr
and
.Li os
capabilities of the PMC also scope the branch records: user-only
sampling suppresses branches ending in CPL 0 and system-only sampling
suppresses branches ending in CPL greater than 0.
.Pp
Samples taken with LBR active set the PMC_CC_F_MULTIPART flag and
embed a payload of type PMC_CC_MULTIPART_LBR in the callchain record,
using the layout described in
.Xr pmc.ibs 3 .
The payload holds the valid branch records, most recent branch first,
as two 64-bit words per record: the raw From then To register image.
The instruction pointer is bits [57:0] of each word, sign-extended
from bit 57; bit 63 of the From word flags a mispredicted branch;
bit 62 of the To word flags a speculative record.
Invalid records are dropped in the kernel and do not appear in the
payload.
.Sh CAVEATS
The branch-type filter register and the ring itself are shared per
CPU; when several LBR PMCs are scheduled on the same CPU the most
recently started one determines the filter, and a process-scope PMC
wipes the ring on every context switch-in, discarding records a
concurrent system-scope PMC had accumulated there.
.Pp
For system-wide PMCs the ring is not cleared on context switches, so
a sample taken shortly after a switch can include branches from the
previous address space.
Process-mode PMCs get a clean ring on every switch-in.
.Pp
On CPUs without the LbrAndPmcFreeze feature the ring keeps running
until the interrupt handler reads it, so records may include kernel
interrupt-entry branches.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pmc 3 ,
.Xr pmc.amd 3 ,
.Xr pmc.ibs 3 ,
.Xr pmclog 3 ,
.Xr hwpmc 4
.Pp
The record format is described in the
.Rs
.%B "Processor Programming Reference (PPR) for AMD Family 19h Model 11h"
.%N "Publication No. 55901"
.%Q "Advanced Micro Devices, Inc."
.Re
.Sh HISTORY
LBR v2 capture support was first introduced in
.Fx 16.0 .
